  "title": "dcm: Don't recreate fixed hashmaps every dissection",
  "description": "The hash maps in DCM are based on constant structs and are never\nchanged during dissection, only used for lookups.\nDo not recreate them every dissection; create them in epan scope.\n\nIn actuality, these should either use binary search (the two that\nuse integers keys could do that easily) or tools/make-packet-dcm.py\nshould use a perfect hash function generator like GNU gperf rather\nthan inserting these into a map on startup.\n\nFixup ba9aa3015f29f07bf81cdfebdfab54fdc379b94d",
